{# WHO THIS INSTALLATION BELONGS TO.

   EVERY FIELD STATES ITS CONSEQUENCE, which is the whole reason the third
   column is there: somebody deciding whether to set a logo needs to know what
   happens if they do not, and somebody reading the time zone needs to know
   that every instant on every screen is read in it.

   A FRESH INSTALLATION HAS BEEN GIVEN NO NAME, and the screen says so rather
   than inventing one: the name falls back to the wordmark it was shipped
   with and every other field reads "not set". That is the page telling
   somebody exactly what there is to do.

   DRAWN TO ITS SCOPE, NOT TO ITS FULL DEPTH (ruled 2026-09-20). The fields
   are settled; the editing form, the logo upload and who may change any of it
   are queued, and the hint says so. #}
{% extends '@Shell/settings/_section.html.twig' %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {%- set identity = settings.identity -%}
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Identity<span class="src">&middot; what the organization is called, and how it is drawn</span></span>
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <td>Name</td>
                <td><b>{{ identity.name }}</b></td>
                <td class="mono fog">shown in the header and on every export</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Short name</td>
                <td>{% if identity.shortName %}<b>{{ identity.shortName }}</b>{% else %}<span class="w">not set</span>{% endif %}</td>
                <td class="mono fog">used where the full name will not fit</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Logo</td>
                <td>{% if identity.logo %}<b>{{ identity.logo }}</b>{% else %}<span class="w">not set</span>{% endif %}</td>
                <td class="mono fog">falls back to the wordmark</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Time zone</td>
                <td>
                    {%- if identity.timeZone -%}
                        <b>{{ identity.timeZone }}</b>
                        {%- set offset = identity.utcOffset(date()) -%}
                        {%- if offset %} <span class="mono">{{ offset }}</span>{% endif -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        <span class="w">not set</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                </td>
                <td class="mono fog">every instant on every screen is read in the viewer’s zone</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Country</td>
                <td>{% if identity.country %}<b>{{ identity.country }}</b>{% else %}<span class="w">not set</span>{% endif %}</td>
                <td class="mono fog">the map’s default extent</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'This tab is drawn to its scope, not to its full depth.',
        say: 'The fields above are settled and each states its consequence. Still to draw: the editing form itself, the logo upload, and who may change any of it.',
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
